DOCX: INCLUDETEXT is a file-linked section, saved back as INCLUDETEXT

Word's INCLUDETEXT came in as an unhandled fieldmark with its cached
text: it never read its file, and Ely's .uno:ElyUpdateLinks (0086) saw
no link. The .doc filter has always made a file-linked section.
- After DOCX import, an INCLUDETEXT field that holds whole paragraphs
  becomes a protected file-linked section: its file (relative to the
  document) and bookmark become the link; the cached text stays shown
  until the user updates links. A field beside other text in its
  paragraph stays a field: a section holds whole paragraphs.
- Word export writes a file-linked section as an INCLUDETEXT field:
  it begins at the section's first paragraph and ends at its last, the
  section's text as the field result.
- DeleteFieldmarkCommand and IsInsRegionAvailable are exported for the
  filter library.

